  "step_3": "The decision reason requires evaluating and preferring the more right-skewed lottery (Lottery A). However, the individual explicitly prefers Lottery B because it has a higher chance of yielding a non-zero outcome—this is the opposite of what a right-skewness preference would imply. The information considered by the individual (probability of winning something) is not aligned with the information relevant to skewness (distribution of probabilities across favorable vs. unfavorable outcomes, particularly concentration on low outcomes). Furthermore, the individual’s justification is based on maximizing the chance of a non-zero gain, which favors left-skewed or less skewed distributions, not more right-skewed ones. There is no indication that the individual assessed the skewness of the lotteries or used it in their reasoning. Therefore, the decision reason was not used.",
  "final_assessment_score": 0
