  "step_1": "The decision reason is based on skewness, specifically preferring the lottery that is more right-skewed, defined as assigning a greater portion of probability to unfavorable outcomes compared to favorable ones. In this context, 'unfavorable' outcomes are lower or zero payoffs, and 'favorable' are the positive payoffs. For Lottery A: 3000 Euros with 0.2% probability (favorable), 0 Euros with 99.8% (unfavorable). For Lottery B: 6000 Euros with 0.1% (favorable), 0 Euros with 99.9% (unfavorable). The probability mass on unfavorable outcomes (i.e., 0 Euros) is 99.8% for A and 99.9% for B. Thus, B assigns a slightly greater portion of probability to the unfavorable outcome than A. Therefore, B is more right-skewed than A. The decision reason would prefer B over A because it is more right-skewed. The reason is applicable because skewness can be determined from the given probabilities and outcomes.",
